```sjs
context.LocalComputed.CertainParameters = "Certain parameters"
context.LocalComputed.TheseParameters = "These parameters"
context.LocalComputed.TheseGlobalValues = "These global values"
context.LocalComputed.Defaults = "defaults"
context.LocalComputed.Them = "them"
context.LocalComputed.Parameters = "parameters"
context.LocalComputed.Are = "are"
if (context.Local.ParameterLen == 1) {
  context.LocalComputed.CertainParameters = "A parameter"
  context.LocalComputed.TheseParameters = "This parameter"
  context.LocalComputed.TheseGlobalValues = "This global value"
  context.LocalComputed.Defaults = "the default"
  context.LocalComputed.Them = "it"
  context.LocalComputed.Parameters = "parameter"
  context.LocalComputed.Are = "is"
}
sjs```

`{{sanitizeCliName}} configure` stores your settings in `~/.config/{{sanitizeCliName}}/config.yaml`. You can run it interactively to set credentials and persistent preferences, or edit the config file directly.

For authentication credentials specifically, see [Authentication](#authentication).

### Global Parameters

{{.LocalComputed.CertainParameters}} {{.LocalComputed.Are}} configured globally and applied to all commands that use {{.LocalComputed.Them}}. {{.LocalComputed.TheseParameters}} can be set via CLI flags, environment variables, or the config file. Individual commands can override global values with their own flags when needed.

Priority: CLI flags > environment variables > config file

| Source | Example |
|--------|---------|
| CLI flag | `{{sanitizeCliName}} {{templateGlobalFlagExample}} {{templateGlobalExampleCommand}}` |
{{- if .Global.Config.EnvVarPrefix }}
| Environment variable | `{{templateGlobalEnvVarExample}} {{sanitizeCliName}} {{templateGlobalExampleCommand}}` |
{{- end}}
| Config file | `{{sanitizeCliName}} configure` |

#### Available Global Parameters

{{templateCLIGlobalsTable}}

### Example

```bash
# Set a global parameter via flag
{{sanitizeCliName}} {{templateGlobalFlagExample}} {{templateGlobalExampleCommand}}
{{- if .Global.Config.EnvVarPrefix }}

# Or set via environment variable
{{templateGlobalEnvVarExample}} {{sanitizeCliName}} {{templateGlobalExampleCommand}}
{{- end}}

# Or configure globally (persisted to config file)
{{sanitizeCliName}} configure
```
